# MongoDB Connection String
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your MongoDB Atlas connection string
#
# Steps to get connection string:
# 1. Go to https://www.mongodb.com/cloud/atlas
# 2. Sign up (free account)
# 3. Create free cluster (M0 tier)
# 4. Create database user (username + password)
# 5. Allow network access (Allow from anywhere)
# 6. Click "Connect" → "Connect your application"
# 7. Copy connection string
# 8. Replace <password> with your password
# 9. Add /medical at the end (database name)
#
# Format:
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://username:password@cluster.mongodb.net/medical?retryWrites=true&w=majority
#
# Example:
# MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://medical-user:MyPassword123@cluster0.abc123.mongodb.net/medical?retryWrites=true&w=majority

